## 1 Commitments

Three to five sentences, each one a promise a reviewer can hold a screen to.
Write the ones this product would actually be judged on, not a general list.

- Nothing that takes longer than a moment happens without the surface saying so.
- A destructive action is always recoverable, or always confirmed. Never neither.
- <commitment specific to this product>

## 2 State patterns

Every surface owes an answer to each row. "Not applicable" is an answer and
needs a reason.

| State | What the surface owes | Copy pattern |
|---|---|---|
| Empty, first use | What this is for and the one action that fills it | |
| Empty, filtered to nothing | That the filter caused it, and the way back | |
| Loading, under a moment | Nothing. Do not flash a spinner | — |
| Loading, longer | Progress if it is knowable, a skeleton if it is not | |
| Partial | What arrived, what did not, whether it will retry itself | |
| Offline | What still works, what is queued | |
| Error, the user can fix it | What happened and the next action, in that order | |
| Error, the user cannot fix it | What happened, what is being done, what to do meanwhile | |
| Success, in place | The change itself, visible. A toast only if it left the view | |

## 3 Interaction primitives

The behaviours that repeat across surfaces, decided once.

| Primitive | Rule |
|---|---|
| Primary action per view | One. If two compete, one is not primary |
| Destructive action | <confirm, or undo window of N seconds — pick one and say which> |
| Undo | <where it lives, how long it lasts> |
| Selection | <single or multi, what clears it> |
| Navigation away with unsaved work | <blocked, autosaved, or discarded — say which> |
| Keyboard | Every action reachable without a pointer; focus visible at all times |
| Focus after an action | <where focus lands after create, delete, close> |
| Form validation | <on blur, on submit — and never only on submit> |

## 4 Voice and tone

How the product speaks. Give real strings, not adjectives.

- **Register**: <plain, warm, terse — one word, then an example>
